its screen, it can take c6. Using g6 as its screen, it can take i6. - **Why not
车8平6 to chase the cannon:** red would reply 炮四平七 and take c6. From c6 the
cannon eyes the elephant on c9, and it can still take g6 with e6 as the screen.
That could cost two pawns. It is also easy to walk into danger around the
elephant on c9 and the king. - **Why 卒3进1:** it steps the 3-file pawn out of
the cannon's line. On c5 it is protected by the elephant on e7, and it opens
the d5 and b5 squares for the horse on c7. - **If red takes i6:** the cannon
lands on the edge. Its only follow-up target is e6, which both horses protect.
I can then play 车8平9 to chase it and gain a tempo. } 8. 车一平二 卒７进１ {
